IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ia-types`
IMPORT `ia-penalties`
IMPORT `ia-permission`
IMPORT `ia-supervision`
IMPORT `ia-policies`

-- Insurance Act 1966 — THE TOP-LEVEL GOALS.
--
-- The Act speaks to two audiences, and each has one question:
--
--   TOP-LEVEL GOAL A, the regulated person:
--     "For this person and what it does, does the Insurance Act reach it,
--      does it permit it, and if not, what offence is it and what is the
--      most it can cost?"  — Goals 1-4 (ss 3-92, 142-145).
--
--   TOP-LEVEL GOAL B, the policy:
--     "For this policy and its owner, what kind of policy is it, is it
--      valid and for how much, what rights does the owner have, and who
--      receives the death benefits?"  — Goals 6-7 (ss 3, 66-68, 131-152,
--      First Schedule).
--
-- Goal 5 (supervision, appeals, transfers, winding up) answers its own dated
-- questions in `ia-supervision.l4`.

§ `The top-level goals`

§§ `A — the regulated person`

DECLARE `Regulatory position` HAS
    `the Act reaches the act`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `permitted`                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `the offence if not permitted`           IS A MAYBE `IA offence`
    `maximum penalty`                        IS A MAYBE `IA penalty`
    `most that may be collected to compound` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `triable by`                             IS A LIST OF STRING

@ref ss 3-92, 138, 142-145
GIVEN c IS A `Regulatory case`
GIVETH A `Regulatory position`
`the regulatory position for` c MEANS
    `Regulatory position` WITH
        `the Act reaches the act`                IS `reached`
        `permitted`                              IS `ok`
        `the offence if not permitted`           IS IF `ok` THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST `offence`
        `maximum penalty`                        IS
            IF `ok` OR NOT `reached` THEN NOTHING
            ELSE JUST (`the maximum penalty for` `offence` `, an individual:` (s's `an individual`) `, a corporation:` (NOT s's `an individual`))
        `most that may be collected to compound` IS
            IF `ok` OR NOT `reached` THEN NOTHING
            ELSE `the most that may be collected to compound` `offence` `, an individual:` (s's `an individual`) `, prescribed:` (c's `prescribed as a compoundable offence`)
        `triable by`                             IS `the courts that may try an offence and impose the full penalty`
    WHERE
        s MEANS c's `person`
        a MEANS c's `activity`
        `ok` MEANS `the activity is permitted` s a
        `offence` MEANS `the offence for` a
        `reached` MEANS `the Act reaches an act` (c's `place`) `, an offence under s 4, 8, 70 or 75:` (`an offence under s 4, 8, 70 or 75` a)

§§ `B — the policy`

DECLARE `Policy position` HAS
    `Singapore or offshore`                  IS A STRING
    `class of business`                      IS A `Class of business`
    `the person had capacity to insure`      IS A BOOLEAN
    `valid for insurable interest`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `most that may be recovered`             IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `the owner's statutory rights`           IS A LIST OF STRING
    `the death benefits go`                  IS A STRING
    `the insurer may pay without probate`    IS A STRING

@ref ss 3, 66, 132, 133, 146-151, 150; First Schedule
GIVEN p IS A `Policy case`, e IS AN `Estate facts`
GIVETH A `Policy position`
`the policy position for` p `, estate` e MEANS
    `Policy position` WITH
        `Singapore or offshore`               IS `the policy is` p
        `class of business`                   IS `the class of business of` p
        `the person had capacity to insure`   IS `has capacity to insure, aged` (p's `age of the person entering the contract`) `, with a parent's written consent:` (p's `written consent of a parent or guardian`)
        `valid for insurable interest`        IS `the policy is valid for insurable interest` p
        `most that may be recovered`          IS `the most that may be recovered under` p
        `the owner's statutory rights`        IS `the owner's statutory rights under` p
        `the death benefits go`               IS IF p's `kind` EQUALS `a general insurance policy` THEN "not a life or accident and health policy: Part 3C does not apply" ELSE `the death benefits go` e
        `the insurer may pay without probate` IS IF p's `kind` EQUALS `a general insurance policy` THEN "not a life or accident and health policy: s 150 does not apply" ELSE `the insurer may pay without probate` e
